      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## Automated image upscaling & embedding watermarks on property photos\n\n### How it works\n\nThe workflow triggers automatically when a new file appears in a specified Google Drive folder.\nIt checks a Google Sheet and evaluates conditions before proceeding to download and extract the file contents.\nExtracted data is sent to a Generative Language API, returning content that is then converted to a file.\nA separate HTTP request fetches a logo image, which is applied as a watermark using calculated dimensions.\nFinally, the watermarked image is uploaded back to Google Drive and the operation is recorded as a new row in Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Connect your Google Drive account for the trigger, download, and upload nodes.\n- [ ] Authenticate your Google Sheets account and choose the correct document for both checking and appending.\n- [ ] Add your Google Generative Language API key to the HTTP Request node.\n- [ ] Verify the direct URL for your watermark logo in the secondary HTTP Request node.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can change the watermark logo by replacing the image URL in the HTTP Request node and tweak the position logic in the JavaScript Code node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
